FLOPPY from to   (as COPY: A, DFA or FDA the first floppy; B, DFB or FDB)
FLOPPY A
  The floppy disc's files: names, sizes, its format.
FLOPPY A GAMES   FLOPPY A IDE:GAMES/X   FLOPPY A C:
  Each file copied into the folder (made if it isn't there - UniDOS), or a
  drive (a RAM disc ...).
FLOPPY A GAME.DSK   FLOPPY A IDE:IMGS/GAME.DSK
  The whole disc as a .DSK image (extended): each track's sectors as read,
  tracks 0-39 (40, 41 when formatted).
FLOPPY GAMES A   FLOPPY C: A
  Each file in the folder (or drive) onto the disc: added to its files (one
  of the same name replaced), an AMSDOS header with it.
FLOPPY GAME.DSK A
  The image onto the disc: each track formatted as the image has it, then
  its sectors written. One side, 42 tracks at most.
  The controller itself does it (not AMSDOS or UniDOS): data (C1-C9),
  system (41-49) and IBM (01-08) formats. It claims the controller (FDC
  0) first: another program's claim on it is refused until FLOPPY ends.
